\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-build-button-chain implementation -p 8.1: \"Implement the HTML as a small self-contained document. Store the generated-button count in script state, append a single new button only when event.target is the current last button, and replace document.body content with a single finished-state element on the fourth generated-button click.\" -p 8.2: \"Edge cases: clicking an older button must do nothing, rapid repeated clicks must not append more than one button per accepted click, and the terminal state must remove the chain rather than leaving hidden or stale buttons.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-build-button-chain goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \"N/A: this goal owns three work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain current-state -p 2.1: \"This goal begins after the future implementation file exists. During this planning proof, all verification steps remain planned instructions only and are not executed.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain why -p 4.1: \"The benchmark behavior is observable in a browser and has edge cases that source text alone can miss. This goal produces independent proof for semantics, user interaction, and planning-only artifact hygiene.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: static implementation review, one direct browser story for the button chain, and an artifact audit for this planning proof.\" -p 5.2: \"Out of scope: changing button-chain.html, weakening acceptance criteria, using console or DOM injection as UI evidence, or testing during this planning-only benchmark run.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain affected-areas -p 6.1: \"Verification targets are the implemented button-chain.html behavior, the US-01 browser run cache, and the isolated benchmark workspace artifact set.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain dependencies -p 7.1: \"Depends on 01-build-button-chain. W04 consumes W01-W03, W05 consumes W04, and W06 consumes the completed proof artifacts and browser-story outcome.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain implementation -p 8.1: \"Run W04 before browser testing to catch obvious semantic drift. Run US-01 only through user-facing clicks, then audit the planning proof workspace for forbidden HTML artifacts and required reports.\" -p 8.2: \"If US-01 fails after implementation, record the failure in bugs.md, add investigation and fix goals, and rerun the story after the fix rather than changing the story to match the bug.\"\n\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \"N/A: this goal owns three work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\"\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
